    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "why-prefix-sum",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "3. Why Do We Need Prefix Sum?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Now that we know *how* to build a prefix sum array, let's understand *why* we need it. What makes it so powerful?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Imagine you are running an online store, and you have an array storing your daily sales. Suddenly, a manager asks you: *'What was the total sum of sales from Day L to Day R?'*"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If we do not use prefix sums, we must run a loop starting from index `L` all the way to `R`, adding the values one-by-one. This takes **O(N)** time in the worst case because we might need to scan the entire array."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If the manager asks this question **Q times** for different ranges, running a loop every single time will take **O(Q * N)** operations, which is extremely slow."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "id": "sales-query-comparison-drawing"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "With our precalculated **Prefix Sum** array `P`, we can answer any range sum query in a single subtraction: **O(1) Constant Time**! The formula is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "style": "tip",
      "text": "For any query from index L to R:\n· If L > 0: Range Sum = P[R] - P[L - 1]\n· If L = 0: Range Sum = P[R]"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Let's check this formula! What is the sum of elements from index `1` to `3` in our original array `A = [2, 4, 1, 5, 3]`?\n· Using a loop: `4 + 1 + 5 = 10`.\n· Using our formula: `P[3] - P[0] = 12 - 2 = 10`.\nIt matches perfectly, and we didn't run any loop! We just looked at two slots in our prefix sum array."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "complexity",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "4. Complexity Analysis"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity_card",
      "timeComplexity": "O(N)",
      "timeExplanation": "We loop through the original array exactly once to fill the prefix sum array.",
      "spaceComplexity": "O(N)",
      "spaceExplanation": "We allocate a new array of size N to store the cumulative sums."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "common-mistakes",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "5. Common Mistakes to Avoid"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "· **Off-by-One Boundaries**: When answering a query from `L` to `R`, always remember that if `L > 0`, we subtract `P[L - 1]`. If you subtract `P[L]`, you will accidentally exclude `A[L]` from the sum!"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "· **Index Out of Bounds**: If `L = 0`, accessing `P[L - 1]` means accessing `P[-1]`, which will crash your program. Always include an `if` condition to handle `L = 0` as a special case."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
