        "O(1)",
        "O(R - L)"
      ],
      "correctAnswerIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "question": "If you want to find the sum of elements from index 2 to index 5 (inclusive) in array A, what is the correct formula using the prefix sum array P?",
      "options": [
        "P[5] - P[2]",
        "P[5] - P[1]",
        "P[5] - P[0]",
        "P[4] - P[1]"
      ],
      "correctAnswerIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "summary",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "7. Summary"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Let's summarize: A prefix sum array stores cumulative sums from the beginning of the array. Building a prefix sum array takes **O(N)** time and **O(N)** extra space. Once built, it lets us query any range sum in **O(1)** time using `P[R] - P[L - 1]`. Remember to handle the boundary case when `L = 0` to avoid errors!"
    }
  ]
}
